# Zone 1, room 6: Wall-jump dash. Phase 1 grey box.
# BUILD.md s5 tech 6: "wall-jump, then dash, then wall-cling the next wall. Taught by a shaft"; s5
# Wall-jump "794 u/s up, 480 u/s away; 5 f of locked direction ... Resets double jump and air dash";
# s5 Dash "8-way in air".
#
# Layout. The corridor from the west door opens into a shaft 640 u (20 tiles) wide. Its walls are
# smooth but for four clingable bands, each 128 u (4 tiles) tall, on alternate walls, their bottoms
# 384 u apart: band 0 on the east wall 128..256 u above the floor, band 1 on the west wall
# 512..640 u, band 2 east 896..1024 u, band 3 west 1280..1408 u. The exit floor, the east wall's
# top, is 1632 u up; its corridor leads to the east door.
#
# Stand-ins: none needed.
#
# How it teaches. A jump from the floor reaches band 0 across the shaft. Each crossing is the tech:
# the wall-jump away from the cling (it gives the air dash back), the dash diagonally up toward the
# next wall at the wall-jump's top, the air jump at the dash's top, and the cling on the next band
# (the first cling since the wall-jump gives both back again). The first crossing is over the floor,
# where a miss costs only a fall; the fourth lands on the exit floor.
#
# Why this way (every number measured: docs/feel_log/2026-10-19-zone1-b.md). A band is too
# short to climb on its own (kicking past its top meets smooth wall), so each must be left for the
# next one across the shaft. Without the dash the farthest crossing (a kick from the band's top and
# the air jump on the tick that carries furthest; a wall-jump carries 40 u less) meets the far wall
# 69 u too low for the next band (tests/replay/zone1/06_control_no_dash_crossing); with the dash the
# teaching route meets each next wall 84 to 93 u inside its band's reach (387 u above the cling it
# left; the best dash crossing measured, a kick, the air jump and an up-dash, 508 u). One Ember
# Toss does carry a no-dash crossing: thrown up and away from the top of band 0 with an air jump
# it reaches band 1 (a grid search of 576 plans), so the 69 u shortfall above holds for a crossing
# without the toss. The toss's landing trick (the ember thrown from above band 0, a fall to the
# floor, the teleport 400 u up) reaches band 2, and the crossing from there falls 74 u short of
# band 3 (06_control_no_dash_toss). A toss per crossing, waiting its 12 s out on a band between
# them, is not modelled here: docs/adr/0015 records that no room can rule it out.
room zone1/06_wall_jump_dash
size 60 62
spawn 74 1888
